# Provenance pin for the vendored Orca web client in dist/.
#
# dist/ is a BUILD, not source: it is the upstream Orca web client (MIT, github.com/
# stablyai/orca) plus the local patches described in README.md, PII-scrubbed. Because a
# build has no version string inside it, this file is what says which one it is — without
# it, "is the vendored client stale?" and "did something corrupt it?" are both unanswerable.
#
# bin/verify-web-bundle.sh checks dist/ against these values. apps/orca/install.sh runs it
# before serving, so a truncated or half-copied bundle fails the install instead of
# serving a client that loads to a blank page.
#
# When you re-derive dist/ from a newer upstream, update every field here in the same
# commit — a stale pin is worse than no pin.

